hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-36 = unlines (cons "*Slave*, through Medieval Latin *sclavus*, is the name of the Slavs, captured and sold in the early Middle Ages. Slavic *slovo* means word. The people of the word became the word for unfree. *Infant* is *in* + *fans*, not speaking. So unfreedom and unspeech are tied in the words twice. Disinhibited speech is the direct path to truth. *Inhibit* is *in* + *habere*, to hold in. Disinhibition is releasing what was held in: the slave's word released, the infant learning to speak. The human superorganism in its infancy is, by the word, a species that hasn't learned to speak yet." nil)
